course: dictionary
lesson: 6984
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change meaning from place to place. Pants is one of them. In the UK, pants are underwear, the clothes you wear under your trousers. In the USA and Canada, pants are trousers, the clothes that cover each leg. The same word can name two different things.
explain: Context tells you which meaning is right. Read «The cartoon turtles stepped out of their shells and walked about in pants.» A real turtle could never wear clothes like that, so this is a silly cartoon, not a real animal. Always ask: which meaning would make sense here?
explain: Pants can also mean rubbish, as in «That film was pants», which is informal British slang. With one word that has three meanings, read the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Pants is a noun, and it is usually plural: a pair of pants.
fact: In the UK, «pants» means underwear worn under your clothes.
fact: In the USA and Canada, «pants» means trousers, clothes that cover each leg.
fact: In UK slang, «pants» means rubbish or very bad.
fact: The NSPCC PANTS rule is a UK safety rule. It teaches that the parts of your body covered by underwear are private, and that you can always say no.
exercise: Sam, from London, says, «I packed a clean pair of pants for the trip.» What are pants here? | *Underwear, worn under your clothes | Rubbish, very bad | A type of pet | Trousers, the clothes that cover each leg
exercise: Mia, from Toronto, says, «I need a new pair of pants for school.» What does she mean? | *Trousers, the clothes that cover each leg | A bird's nest | Rubbish, very bad | Underwear worn under clothes
exercise: «That film was pants.» What does pants mean? | *Rubbish, very bad | Underwear | Very good, the best | Trousers
test: Which country uses pants to mean trousers? | Scotland | *United States | Ireland | Britain
test: What does «wear the pants» mean? | Wear your underwear to bed | Look smart for a party | *Be the boss | Put on your trousers
exam: What does the NSPCC PANTS rule teach you? | Pants means rubbish | Pants are always the best clothes to wear | Always wear trousers in the playground | *The parts of your body covered by underwear are private, and you can say no
